DTSTAMP:20261104T063145Z
UID:5c50f2bf6c811a1712f590abf4c0@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Lectures & Speakers\,Washington\, DC\,United St
 ates
DESCRIPTION:What Do We Mean By Legal Enculturation? Featuring Dr. Mikaela 
 Spruill \, Assistant Professor of Psychology\, School of Interdisciplinary
  Forensics\, Arizona State University Legal Enculturation: Structural‐Le
 vel Influence on Individual‐Level Psychology The law is a prominent inst
 itutional pillar in societal structure\, and psychology has the ability to
  seriously contended with the way the law shapes individuals' views and pe
 rceptions of the world. Join Dr. Mikaela Spruill for an introduction to th
 e theoretical concept of Legal Enculturation—the dynamic process by whic
 h the legal system defines our individual psychologies—offering a new ap
 proach to critically assess human attitudes and behaviors \nCategory: Lect
 ures & Speakers\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/what-do-
 we-mean-by-legal-enculturation
LOCATION:George Washington University\, Washington\, DC
STATUS:CONFIRMED
