UID:9d0b3dce6c1ab28e37e17fab0abf@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Academic\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The 2026 U.S. midterm elections and Taiwan’s 2026 local elec
 tions unfold during landmark democratic anniversaries: the United States
 ’ semiquincentennial and the 30th anniversary of Taiwan’s first direct
  presidential election. These parallel milestones provide a unique lens fo
 r examining how democratic identity\, institutional resilience\, and cross
 ‑Strait geopolitics shape electoral behavior in both polities. In the Un
 ited States\, midterm dynamics reflect heightened economic anxieties\, ris
 ing consumer prices\, shifting partisan narratives\, and growing voter con
 cerns over affordability and foreign policy crises\, including the conflic
 t with Iran. Simultaneously\, Taiwan’s local elections occur ami\nCatego
 ry: Academic\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/taiwan-conf
 erence-bilateral-ballot-boxes-us-midterms-taiwans-local-elections-and-poli
 cy-trajectories
LOCATION:1957 E Street NW\, 1957 E St NW\, Washington DC 20052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/taiwan-conference-bilateral-ballot-boxe
 s-us-midterms-taiwans-local-elections-and-policy-trajectories
